02:48:25,900 --> 02:48:26,980
Man, I was fast enough.

2734
02:48:28,260 --> 02:48:29,120
But I guess I wasn't.

2735
02:48:29,420 --> 02:48:30,720
So I was not fast enough.

2736
02:48:32,060 --> 02:48:35,200
If you think about it, that sentence makes no sense when you say it like that, the way I just did.

2737
02:48:39,960 --> 02:48:40,840
Okay, you need to die.

2738
02:48:54,940 --> 02:48:56,960
Massive elevators we can utilize as well, if need be.

2739
02:48:58,100 --> 02:48:58,760
Look at that.

2740
02:49:00,960 --> 02:49:02,000
This is actually money.

2741
02:49:02,240 --> 02:49:04,920
Because we can give this to the villager and receive money in return.

2742
02:49:08,280 --> 02:49:11,920
Like, before that, I just thought, oh, diamonds are like, eh, I have so many of them.

2743
02:49:12,420 --> 02:49:13,800
You know, I'm too good for diamonds.

2744
02:49:15,000 --> 02:49:16,860
But now they sort of have a use again.

2745
02:49:18,100 --> 02:49:19,140
Now that I know I can do that.

2746
02:49:31,890 --> 02:49:33,410
I see more diamonds.

2747
02:49:37,090 --> 02:49:41,450
But wait, I'm actually really in... Oh, I have fortune 3 on this, nice.

2748
02:49:43,010 --> 02:49:45,030
So I should be getting a lot of diamonds.

2749
02:50:01,750 --> 02:50:03,450
The bow is the best weapon in the game.

2750
02:50:03,570 --> 02:50:04,030
Change my mind.

2751
02:50:09,510 --> 02:50:11,230
Ah, properly upgraded, that is.

2752
02:50:20,130 --> 02:50:24,030
These things get so bugged on the spikes here.

2753
02:50:24,630 --> 02:50:26,470
On the stalagmites.

2754
02:50:30,460 --> 02:50:31,580
Yep, that's right.

2755
02:50:31,780 --> 02:50:33,000
Your boy used the right word.

2756
02:50:35,940 --> 02:50:39,660
Oh my god.

2757
02:50:40,420 --> 02:50:41,380
Get up here.

2758
02:50:42,340 --> 02:50:43,820
Get that diamond.

2759
02:50:47,100 --> 02:50:49,000
And then put it in my belly.

2760
02:50:49,640 --> 02:50:54,560
Just open me up surgically and insert the diamonds right into my tummy.

2761
02:50:56,160 --> 02:50:57,180
I would love that.

2762
02:51:12,800 --> 02:51:13,240
Nice.

2763
02:51:13,240 --> 02:51:14,460
I see more diamonds.

2764
02:51:16,500 --> 02:51:17,300
Okay, okay!

2765
02:51:18,580 --> 02:51:20,140
Oh man, I don't know if I should do this.

2766
02:51:28,810 --> 02:51:29,410
Wait, wait, wait.

2767
02:51:29,490 --> 02:51:31,170
I don't know if it works if it's not a source.

2768
02:51:33,530 --> 02:51:34,310
No, wait.

2769
02:51:34,510 --> 02:51:35,570
I don't trust this.

2770
02:51:36,350 --> 02:51:38,270
I don't know if this works if it's not a source.

2771
02:51:38,390 --> 02:51:39,230
Like, this is a source.

2772
02:51:40,150 --> 02:51:40,810
This is not.

2773
02:51:42,210 --> 02:51:43,390
No, I'm not doing it.

2774
02:51:43,730 --> 02:51:44,510
I'm not doing it.

2775
02:51:45,830 --> 02:51:46,430
No way.

2776
02:51:48,350 --> 02:51:49,430
I do want to go down, though.

2777
02:51:49,950 --> 02:51:51,010
Actually, okay, check this out.

2778
02:51:51,110 --> 02:51:52,890
You want to see the craziest moves of all time?

2779
02:51:55,410 --> 02:51:56,590
Let me plan this.

2780
02:51:57,980 --> 02:51:58,940
Okay.

2781
02:51:59,760 --> 02:52:00,580
Here we go.

2782
02:52:07,000 --> 02:52:11,980
Oh my god!

2783
02:52:15,640 --> 02:52:17,040
Insane.

2784
02:52:19,660 --> 02:52:21,060
Scary!

2785
02:52:23,020 --> 02:52:25,880
You're a scary skeletonos.

2786
02:52:30,410 --> 02:52:31,110
I see you.

2787
02:52:32,590 --> 02:52:33,670
And a peekaboo!

2788
02:52:33,930 --> 02:52:34,490
Oh, shit.

2789
02:52:35,430 --> 02:52:36,190
There we go.

2790
02:52:36,730 --> 02:52:37,130
Easy.

2791
02:52:39,410 --> 02:52:40,550
What's hiding in here, then?

2792
02:52:45,500 --> 02:52:55,940
Like, I did say I was not gonna go caving without my crazy good pickaxe, you know, with efficiency on it and all that, but... I'm not mining iron.

2793
02:52:56,120 --> 02:52:59,660
I'm just sort of, you know, floating through space and time.

2794
02:53:00,700 --> 02:53:05,940
Loving my life and just having a grand old journey, you know?

2795
02:53:07,500 --> 02:53:08,680
It's like lounging.

2796
02:53:10,020 --> 02:53:11,680
Lounging on the couch.

2797
02:53:12,340 --> 02:53:13,440
There's no real...

2798
02:53:13,560 --> 02:53:16,060
Purpose, it's just, you're just there, you know, in the moment.

2799
02:53:16,680 --> 02:53:18,120
Doing the act of lounging.

2800
02:53:18,740 --> 02:53:23,720
And that's the same thing I'm doing here, but... Just killing things and exploring a little bit.

2801
02:53:23,920 --> 02:53:24,080
Oh!

2802
02:53:25,020 --> 02:53:25,760
Where's my shield?

2803
02:53:28,320 --> 02:53:28,740
What?!

2804
02:53:28,740 --> 02:53:31,800
This guy's immune to arrows!

2805
02:53:37,000 --> 02:53:37,420
Insane!

2806
02:53:40,370 --> 02:53:40,570
Wow!

2807
02:53:40,710 --> 02:53:42,190
Wow, that actually hurts a lot.

2808
02:53:43,950 --> 02:53:44,750
Bastards.

2809
02:53:46,790 --> 02:53:47,590
Hmm.

2810
02:53:48,790 --> 02:54:00,850
You know... I could technically bring these stalagmites with me and make a perimeter around my home of stalagmites.

2811
02:54:04,070 --> 02:54:05,410
What is this music?

2812
02:54:11,500 --> 02:54:13,320
Yo, I've never heard this one.

2813
02:54:21,500 --> 02:54:22,400
That's nice.

2814
02:54:33,520 --> 02:54:38,840
How does this game keep dishing up new music?

2815
02:54:50,030 --> 02:54:54,390
Speaking of lounging, allow me a moment here.

2816
02:55:43,420 --> 02:55:45,140
I call that the instant shower.

2817
02:55:46,180 --> 02:55:54,420
If you're in a hurry, and you're lounging, and you don't have time for that, you just quickly go through the water, you know?

2818
02:55:56,100 --> 02:55:58,640
As long as the water touches your body, it counts.

2819
02:55:58,820 --> 02:55:59,380
You have showered.

2820
02:56:03,970 --> 02:56:06,670
I don't know, that was like an impulsive thought.

2821
02:56:06,930 --> 02:56:09,490
I couldn't get it out, you know?

2822
02:56:10,390 --> 02:56:11,710
I just had to do something.

2823
02:56:12,650 --> 02:56:14,150
There was a feeling inside of me.

2824
02:56:15,670 --> 02:56:17,970
And it swelled up, and I just had to act on it.

2825
02:56:18,030 --> 02:56:18,450
I'm sorry.

2826
02:56:19,910 --> 02:56:20,790
It just happens.

2827
02:56:23,670 --> 02:56:24,250
What's this?

2828
02:56:28,950 --> 02:56:29,950
More mines.

2829
02:56:31,630 --> 02:56:32,870
I yearn for it.

2830
02:56:35,890 --> 02:56:37,170
I'm taking that too.

2831
02:56:44,550 --> 02:56:46,370
Dude, this song is fantastic.

2832
02:57:04,600 --> 02:57:05,760
We're back in the mines.

2833
02:57:14,120 --> 02:57:15,640
Oh man, it's so dark.

2834
02:57:20,660 --> 02:57:22,380
Will I ever find what I'm looking for?

2835
02:57:28,820 --> 02:57:30,060
What am I looking for?

2836
02:57:34,830 --> 02:57:35,670
Who am I?

2837
02:57:43,930 --> 02:57:45,030
Okay, that's a dead end.

2838
02:57:45,250 --> 02:57:45,490
Fuck.

2839
02:57:52,170 --> 02:57:53,090
Level 39.

2840
02:57:59,090 --> 02:58:00,470
No, I was not gonna take this now.

2841
02:58:01,450 --> 02:58:02,370
I made a pact.

2842
02:58:03,270 --> 02:58:04,170
I signed it.

2843
02:58:07,430 --> 02:58:08,230
Done and dusted.

2844
02:58:09,730 --> 02:58:12,290
They must have added that song in this update.

2845
02:58:12,650 --> 02:58:13,970
I have never heard that before.

2846
02:58:14,110 --> 02:58:18,430
I mean, chances are I've just been unlucky, I guess, but... That was beautiful.

2847
02:58:20,790 --> 02:58:21,650
Holy shit.

2848
02:58:21,790 --> 02:58:23,470
And I thought I heard every track in this game.

2849
02:58:31,320 --> 02:58:32,220
I need these.

2850
02:58:39,280 --> 02:58:40,740
Ah, here we go.

2851
02:58:40,780 --> 02:58:43,400
I was wondering if I'd see a goddamn minecart.

2852
02:58:47,000 --> 02:58:48,600
Oh, I didn't mean to do that.

2853
02:58:48,880 --> 02:58:49,420
But okay.

2854
02:58:52,040 --> 02:58:53,100
We got breads.

2855
02:58:55,760 --> 02:58:56,740
And... nice.

2856
02:58:57,040 --> 02:58:57,840
A couple more of these.

2857
02:58:58,100 --> 02:58:58,500
Wonderful.

2858
02:59:00,180 --> 02:59:01,100
I can throw that away.

2859
02:59:01,760 --> 02:59:03,120
Let's utilize this guy.

2860
02:59:04,020 --> 02:59:05,700
Ah, this one's almost full.

2861
02:59:06,300 --> 02:59:07,660
I'll bring that with me, why not?

2862
02:59:09,400 --> 02:59:10,800
And a full stack of those.

2863
02:59:12,640 --> 02:59:14,140
Then we're gonna need this chest.

2864
02:59:15,740 --> 02:59:17,260
Fill it up to the brim.

2865
02:59:18,620 --> 02:59:20,240
This bow is not needed.

2866
02:59:21,600 --> 02:59:22,960
Neither is that or that.

2867
02:59:24,320 --> 02:59:26,260
Ah, chestplate obviously is needed.

2868
02:59:38,810 --> 02:59:41,010
Man, what is that song where they go switchback?

2869
02:59:41,670 --> 02:59:43,230
And then something else happens, you know?

2870
02:59:43,750 --> 02:59:45,630
Something musical happens after that.

2871
02:59:46,190 --> 02:59:47,670
But at some point they go switchback.

2872
02:59:52,580 --> 02:59:54,020
Nah, I wasn't gonna mine this.

2873
02:59:54,160 --> 02:59:55,020
I don't know why I keep mining it.

2874
02:59:56,740 --> 02:59:57,100
Okay.

2875
02:59:59,160 --> 02:59:59,840
Let's keep moving.

2876
03:00:01,420 --> 03:00:03,140
I'm not yearning for the mines too much anymore.

2877
03:00:06,580 --> 03:00:06,940
Boom!

2878
03:00:07,160 --> 03:00:08,000
Oh, you didn't die.

2879
03:00:08,780 --> 03:00:09,740
Now I look like a fool.

2880
03:00:19,260 --> 03:00:22,020
Yeah, I yearn for big open spaces like this.

2881
03:00:34,020 --> 03:00:36,820
These guys are so dumb when it comes to stalagmite.

2882
03:00:40,400 --> 03:00:42,940
I can definitely abuse... Oh, actually, hold on a minute.

2883
03:00:44,920 --> 03:00:46,960
Hey, I just had an idea.

2884
03:00:48,500 --> 03:00:49,560
Check this out.

2885
03:00:49,880 --> 03:00:52,240
If I can somehow... Okay, okay, watch this.

2886
03:00:52,580 --> 03:00:54,140
We're gonna have water, right?

2887
03:00:54,460 --> 03:00:57,160
It's gonna push enemies along.

2888
03:00:57,700 --> 03:01:01,340
They're gonna fall into stalagmites.

2889
03:01:01,940 --> 03:01:04,440
AKA old-school spike traps.

2890
03:01:04,860 --> 03:01:05,900
Vietnam-style.

2891
03:01:07,260 --> 03:01:08,260
Jungle tactics.

2892
03:01:13,390 --> 03:01:14,070
Right?

2893
03:01:14,070 --> 03:01:18,810
The only problem is... Well, uh... I'm basically talking about creepers here.

2894
03:01:19,310 --> 03:01:23,090
Still need to find a, uh... creeper spawner.

2895
03:01:25,010 --> 03:01:25,690
Somewhere.

2896
03:01:26,870 --> 03:01:27,890
Let me get up here.

2897
03:01:39,700 --> 03:01:43,340
Man, I'm hoping for some skulk down here.

2898
03:01:45,020 --> 03:01:46,740
It's been ages since I've seen it.

2899
03:01:48,860 --> 03:01:50,700
And I have many things I want to try with it.

2900
03:01:53,500 --> 03:01:54,460
Where is it?

2901
03:02:01,460 --> 03:02:02,460
Okay, we're gonna fly.

2902
03:02:12,600 --> 03:02:15,200
Man, that gets the tummy tickling, doesn't it?

2903
03:02:16,860 --> 03:02:18,220
That's not even a real word, is it?

2904
03:02:18,640 --> 03:02:19,800
Thank you, I needed that.

2905
03:02:22,080 --> 03:02:22,480
Dankeschön.

2906
03:02:22,620 --> 03:02:23,700
I hear a Skeletronus.

2907
03:02:26,340 --> 03:02:27,480
Ah, opening, opening.

2908
03:02:27,640 --> 03:02:28,000
I see it.

2909
03:02:31,840 --> 03:02:32,620
We have done it.

2910
03:02:32,840 --> 03:02:34,460
That was the last... That was perfect.

2911
03:02:34,760 --> 03:02:36,020
The last torch has been utilized.

2912
03:02:48,950 --> 03:02:50,270
I thought I just fell down.

2913
03:02:50,910 --> 03:02:51,890
We're good, we're good.

2914
03:02:53,570 --> 03:02:54,030
Beautiful.

2915
03:02:55,290 --> 03:02:58,050
Nice, but the problem is we only have four rockets left now.

2916
03:03:00,250 --> 03:03:04,950
Question, can I MacGyver something together here to make more?

2917
03:03:05,270 --> 03:03:05,950
Let's see.

2918
03:03:08,430 --> 03:03:09,530
I'm gonna need paper.

2919
03:03:10,630 --> 03:03:12,990
And to make paper, there's multiple ways, right?

2920
03:03:16,370 --> 03:03:17,910
Pa... paper?

2921
03:03:20,750 --> 03:03:21,630
No.

2922
03:03:21,990 --> 03:03:22,850
It's sugarcane.

2923
03:03:23,110 --> 03:03:24,690
It's just straight-up sugarcane.

2924
03:03:27,630 --> 03:03:29,350
Uh... Alright.

2925
03:03:29,690 --> 03:03:30,670
I can find some.

2926
03:03:31,270 --> 03:03:32,390
Shouldn't be too difficult.

2927
03:03:34,430 --> 03:03:39,930
Now, my cows... I do... eh... I am in need of more meat.

2928
03:03:40,770 --> 03:03:41,510
Sorry.

2929
03:03:43,270 --> 03:03:44,150
Yep.

2930
03:03:48,760 --> 03:03:49,700
You need to die.

2931
03:03:52,660 --> 03:03:57,500
Another thing I want to do more of is just pick up a bunch of random flowers so I can color things.

2932
03:03:59,680 --> 03:04:00,500
Which way is home?

2933
03:04:01,620 --> 03:04:02,240
That way.

2934
03:04:07,680 --> 03:04:10,440
Now the mission is to look for sugar.

2935
03:04:12,560 --> 03:04:13,460
I see some there.

2936
03:04:19,210 --> 03:04:20,610
Look at that, that looks nice.

2937
03:04:22,270 --> 03:04:27,990
In fact, I wonder if that is that valley that I saw when I went south the last time.

2938
03:04:28,150 --> 03:04:31,390
That beautiful valley where I want to build an outpost.

2939
03:04:34,650 --> 03:04:36,070
Could very well be up here.

2940
03:04:38,490 --> 03:04:39,510
But that is home.

2941
03:04:44,300 --> 03:04:45,340
Ah, wait, I shouldn't do that.

2942
03:04:45,480 --> 03:04:47,760
Let me actually use the boat right now because I see some sugar cane there.

2943
03:04:48,180 --> 03:04:49,220
I want to grab it.

2944
03:04:50,560 --> 03:04:53,120
And there's no need to just waste rockets at this point.

2945
03:04:57,300 --> 03:04:58,880
Boating is relatively fast.

2946
03:05:06,810 --> 03:05:11,130
Imagine having that one enchant that makes the water freeze.

2947
03:05:11,590 --> 03:05:16,770
You get in a boat, you go on normal water, and Bob's your uncle.

2948
03:05:17,110 --> 03:05:20,510
You can now sip around the world at lightning speed.

2949
03:05:23,050 --> 03:05:23,690
Right?

2950
03:05:24,810 --> 03:05:25,710
That's genius.

2951
03:05:31,160 --> 03:05:33,620
But I haven't seen that enchant in forever, actually.

2952
03:05:36,060 --> 03:05:41,220
Now that I think about it, I haven't seen that in... well, a year ago, I think.

2953
03:05:42,960 --> 03:05:44,060
How did I get that?

2954
03:05:46,320 --> 03:05:50,140
Maybe a random drop off of one of the enemies or something.

2955
03:05:53,200 --> 03:05:54,640
I have nine sugarcane.

2956
03:05:55,580 --> 03:05:59,700
That is two papers... Wait, I get one paper out of this?

2957
03:06:03,800 --> 03:06:04,540
Oh, three!

2958
03:06:04,760 --> 03:06:05,520
Oh, nice!

2959
03:06:06,380 --> 03:06:07,520
Okay, man, we're rolling.

2960
03:06:08,180 --> 03:06:10,120
And then I have a bunch... Oh, yeah!

2961
03:06:12,520 --> 03:06:13,400
Oh, it doesn't matter?

2962
03:06:13,700 --> 03:06:14,120
Oh!

2963
03:06:14,940 --> 03:06:15,620
That's funny.

2964
03:06:16,880 --> 03:06:17,680
Wait a minute, what?

2965
03:06:25,370 --> 03:06:27,650
Why won't it show me the combination?

2966
03:06:30,750 --> 03:06:31,610
Oh, okay.

2967
03:06:31,910 --> 03:06:33,330
So it's like... That's funny.

2968
03:06:35,350 --> 03:06:36,530
27, yes!

2969
03:06:38,390 --> 03:06:39,290
We're so back.

2970
03:06:42,770 --> 03:06:44,030
One paper, put it here.

2971
03:06:53,410 --> 03:06:53,870
Nice.

2972
03:06:54,510 --> 03:06:55,610
I want to take off the shield.

2973
03:06:56,650 --> 03:06:57,950
Oh, look at that view now.

2974
03:06:58,490 --> 03:07:00,510
It's way better without the shield.

2975
03:07:08,410 --> 03:07:09,110
Nothing good.

2976
03:07:09,250 --> 03:07:11,110
I don't see anything of note.

2977
03:07:15,190 --> 03:07:16,250
And... Oh, cave!

2978
03:07:16,910 --> 03:07:17,970
Hold up, hold up.

2979
03:07:23,620 --> 03:07:24,980
Watch the master at work.

2980
03:07:28,380 --> 03:07:28,940
Sweet.

2981
03:07:30,040 --> 03:07:33,840
I need... oh wait, ah... Shield!

2982
03:07:37,800 --> 03:07:38,740
There you are!

2983
03:07:41,620 --> 03:07:42,180
Asshole!

2984
03:07:44,360 --> 03:07:45,640
Give me this guy.

2985
03:07:48,280 --> 03:07:49,120
Here we go.

2986
03:07:55,770 --> 03:07:56,150
Bam.

2987
03:07:56,150 --> 03:07:56,970
And we're back.

2988
03:07:59,370 --> 03:07:59,750
Rockets.

2989
03:08:03,830 --> 03:08:04,370
Peek-a-boo.

2990
03:08:06,790 --> 03:08:07,490
And you're dead.

2991
03:08:09,970 --> 03:08:12,330
Okay, I just want to take a quick peek down here, you know?

2992
03:08:12,950 --> 03:08:13,610
Oh, we gotta spawn.

2993
03:08:13,710 --> 03:08:15,890
Ah, but that's most likely a spider, right?

2994
03:08:15,950 --> 03:08:16,850
That's a spider one.

2995
03:08:20,500 --> 03:08:21,540
Let me go destroy that.

