Okay, wait.

3808
03:58:40,440 --> 03:58:41,140
More speed.

3809
03:58:44,300 --> 03:58:45,140
More speed.

3810
03:58:45,280 --> 03:58:45,820
There's my bridge!

3811
03:58:46,840 --> 03:58:51,800
And... Okay, slowly.

3812
03:58:56,630 --> 03:58:57,710
Speed?

3813
03:58:58,090 --> 03:58:58,990
Speed?

3814
03:58:59,650 --> 03:59:01,050
Up!

3815
03:59:01,890 --> 03:59:03,310
Oh, we're losing height.

3816
03:59:03,610 --> 03:59:05,190
Come on!

3817
03:59:06,830 --> 03:59:08,230
Speed?

3818
03:59:09,050 --> 03:59:09,850
Up!

3819
03:59:15,170 --> 03:59:16,270
Close enough.

3820
03:59:16,590 --> 03:59:17,550
I made it home.

3821
03:59:18,730 --> 03:59:19,570
Close enough.

3822
03:59:21,350 --> 03:59:22,670
Not bad, eh?

3823
03:59:23,750 --> 03:59:24,930
We did it.

3824
03:59:25,410 --> 03:59:26,470
What an expedition.

3825
03:59:30,090 --> 03:59:31,390
Everybody, I'm home.

3826
03:59:33,030 --> 03:59:34,030
Wake up.

3827
03:59:34,450 --> 03:59:35,470
Here they come.

3828
03:59:40,400 --> 03:59:41,300
How y'all doing?

3829
03:59:42,760 --> 03:59:43,960
What do you got for me today?

3830
03:59:46,660 --> 03:59:49,260
Yolanda, I need to level you up.

3831
03:59:50,180 --> 03:59:51,740
You need paper and money.

3832
03:59:53,240 --> 03:59:56,340
Well, I need paper and I also want money.

3833
03:59:57,000 --> 03:59:57,700
Paper is money.

3834
03:59:58,780 --> 03:59:59,780
I need both.

3835
04:00:01,240 --> 04:00:02,420
Yo, Rosie!

3836
04:00:03,640 --> 04:00:04,800
You're over here, aren't you?

3837
04:00:06,400 --> 04:00:07,400
You're not over here.

3838
04:00:07,800 --> 04:00:09,160
Ah, wait, you were on top of the cake.

3839
04:00:10,840 --> 04:00:11,860
You're not on top of the cake.

3840
04:00:13,040 --> 04:00:14,520
I don't know where the fuck Rosie is.

3841
04:00:15,760 --> 04:00:17,640
The 3D audio is... Ah, there you are.

3842
04:00:17,780 --> 04:00:18,560
There you are.

3843
04:00:18,780 --> 04:00:20,000
Look, I brought you something.

3844
04:00:21,060 --> 04:00:22,240
On this trip I was on.

3845
04:00:22,400 --> 04:00:24,940
Look, I brought it on this trip I was on.

3846
04:00:27,680 --> 04:00:31,180
Um... I, uh... Listen.

3847
04:00:32,160 --> 04:00:34,460
Where did I put that thing in my backpack?

3848
04:00:34,620 --> 04:00:34,900
I...

3849
04:00:34,960 --> 04:00:36,040
I think I left it out here.

3850
04:00:36,140 --> 04:00:36,480
One second.

3851
04:00:37,720 --> 04:00:39,900
I brought you something I forgot.

3852
04:00:43,460 --> 04:00:48,060
I'm gonna quickly go get that thing we forgot.

3853
04:00:49,400 --> 04:00:50,280
Very important.

3854
04:00:53,680 --> 04:00:54,380
Oh no.

3855
04:00:57,780 --> 04:00:58,680
Not now.

3856
04:01:02,930 --> 04:01:03,570
360.

3857
04:01:05,490 --> 04:01:12,850
And while we do that, we're gonna get rid of... There we go.

3858
04:01:14,710 --> 04:01:15,350
What?

3859
04:01:16,190 --> 04:01:18,470
Oh, I thought I just got sandstone.

3860
04:01:19,710 --> 04:01:20,350
What?

3861
04:01:21,090 --> 04:01:21,950
Come on.

3862
04:01:22,490 --> 04:01:23,330
One more.

3863
04:01:32,420 --> 04:01:33,260
One more!

3864
04:01:46,640 --> 04:01:48,580
Hey, Rosie, look what I found!

3865
04:01:48,820 --> 04:01:50,380
I mean, uh, in my bag.

3866
04:01:51,440 --> 04:01:52,280
There you go!

3867
04:01:53,440 --> 04:01:54,120
That's for you.

3868
04:01:54,300 --> 04:01:54,920
That's for you.

3869
04:01:55,800 --> 04:01:56,900
Oh, you don't want more?

3870
04:01:57,360 --> 04:01:58,800
Okay, we'll save it for later.

3871
04:02:00,400 --> 04:02:00,960
There we go.

3872
04:02:01,440 --> 04:02:02,360
Two nametacks!

3873
04:02:02,740 --> 04:02:03,600
We gotta use it.

3874
04:02:06,910 --> 04:02:07,390
Donovan?

3875
04:02:08,090 --> 04:02:08,930
Let's see here.

3876
04:02:10,170 --> 04:02:12,170
We should have a... Let's see.

3877
04:02:13,670 --> 04:02:14,650
Oh, I don't know.

3878
04:02:14,790 --> 04:02:15,030
Rick?

3879
04:02:18,890 --> 04:02:22,930
And then we're going to have... Let's see.

3880
04:02:27,310 --> 04:02:27,790
Tegan.

3881
04:02:29,590 --> 04:02:30,510
That's a good name.

3882
04:02:32,930 --> 04:02:34,130
Who doesn't have a name?

3883
04:02:37,300 --> 04:02:38,240
Jane has a name.

3884
04:02:38,540 --> 04:02:40,500
Imagine waking up, someone standing on you.

3885
04:02:40,660 --> 04:02:41,540
Who has a name?

3886
04:02:45,600 --> 04:02:46,800
Yolanda, and this is Jane.

3887
04:02:46,800 --> 04:02:47,760
You don't have a name.

3888
04:02:48,740 --> 04:02:50,360
Okay, he got fed up with that.

3889
04:02:50,700 --> 04:02:52,100
Rick, that's you.

3890
04:02:53,380 --> 04:02:55,260
I dub thee Rick.

3891
04:02:55,800 --> 04:02:56,460
What about you?

3892
04:02:57,220 --> 04:02:58,320
Phyllis, you got a name?

3893
04:03:00,040 --> 04:03:00,660
What about you?

3894
04:03:00,800 --> 04:03:01,160
You have a name?

3895
04:03:01,340 --> 04:03:01,700
You have a name?

3896
04:03:02,260 --> 04:03:02,620
You have a name?

3897
04:03:03,580 --> 04:03:04,760
Okay, you shall be...

3898
04:03:05,490 --> 04:03:05,890
Tegan.

3899
04:03:06,590 --> 04:03:07,250
There you go.

3900
04:03:09,250 --> 04:03:12,810
Slowly but surely, everyone is getting a name and proper identification.

3901
04:03:13,650 --> 04:03:18,590
We're also going to have to issue passports at some point, if they want to travel outside the border of my kingdom.

3902
04:03:18,750 --> 04:03:20,310
I mean, the kingdom we all happen to live in.

3903
04:03:21,350 --> 04:03:22,570
Not that I'm a king or anything.

3904
04:03:23,890 --> 04:03:24,490
Just saying.

3905
04:03:25,570 --> 04:03:25,690
Whoops.

3906
04:03:27,610 --> 04:03:28,470
Take care of these.

3907
04:03:31,710 --> 04:03:32,390
What's that sound?

3908
04:03:39,260 --> 04:03:41,020
Is that not the cutest thing ever?

3909
04:03:45,360 --> 04:03:46,120
So nice.

3910
04:03:46,760 --> 04:03:47,760
Hanging out with Rick.

3911
04:03:48,480 --> 04:03:50,000
Sorry, I didn't mean to push you there.

3912
04:03:50,220 --> 04:03:50,460
Good night.

3913
04:03:51,340 --> 04:03:52,760
I gotta go to sleep as well, man.

3914
04:03:54,640 --> 04:03:56,160
That was a crazy expedition.

3915
04:03:56,460 --> 04:03:57,020
No deaths.

3916
04:03:58,120 --> 04:03:58,540
Wait, did I?

3917
04:03:58,660 --> 04:03:59,260
No, I didn't die.

3918
04:03:59,640 --> 04:04:00,420
Level 40.

3919
04:04:03,260 --> 04:04:06,140
In fact, I was level 42 when I came home, which is kind of magical.

3920
04:04:09,800 --> 04:04:11,020
ODB outside the window.

3921
04:04:11,200 --> 04:04:12,860
He really likes this spot over here.

3922
04:04:13,000 --> 04:04:13,560
Isn't that funny?

3923
04:04:14,760 --> 04:04:16,020
I wonder why that is.

3924
04:04:16,240 --> 04:04:23,360
If there's some part of his programming that tells him to go to a spot initially, and then that is now his spot, you know?

3925
04:04:25,500 --> 04:04:28,100
It's really interesting the way he is always over here.

3926
04:04:29,560 --> 04:04:31,980
Maybe he's longing for something on the other side of this wall.

3927
04:04:33,820 --> 04:04:34,540
Wait a minute.

3928
04:04:35,000 --> 04:04:36,080
Could it be...

3929
04:04:41,780 --> 04:04:43,900
Maybe ODB really likes these bushes.

3930
04:04:46,380 --> 04:04:51,380
I hate these bushes, but... ODB... maybe he loves them.

3931
04:04:55,600 --> 04:04:58,100
Look what I got for you.

3932
04:05:01,220 --> 04:05:02,220
Oh, it's not grown.

3933
04:05:05,580 --> 04:05:07,480
It's gonna be a little defense perimeter, I guess.

3934
04:05:15,090 --> 04:05:15,490
Nice.

3935
04:05:16,690 --> 04:05:17,290
Have fun.

3936
04:05:19,270 --> 04:05:25,450
And I guess since he has the outer shell that is, like, really hard, he's not gonna be affected by the prickly thorns of it.

3937
04:05:26,630 --> 04:05:27,790
Such as myself, you know?

3938
04:05:27,890 --> 04:05:29,350
I have terrible times with that.

3939
04:05:31,690 --> 04:05:32,090
Okay.

3940
04:05:33,010 --> 04:05:34,650
My inventory is a real mess.

3941
04:05:35,830 --> 04:05:40,710
And just like real life with the dishes, I'm just gonna put it off till tomorrow, you know?

3942
04:05:41,330 --> 04:05:41,730
Yeah.

3943
04:05:42,170 --> 04:05:43,590
I'm gonna put it off till next time.

3944
04:05:44,110 --> 04:05:44,730
That's it.

3945
04:05:44,870 --> 04:05:45,950
That was great.

3946
04:05:46,410 --> 04:05:48,670
Play Minecraft, watch Top Gear, get pig?

3947
04:05:49,030 --> 04:05:49,390
Huh?

3948
04:05:50,430 --> 04:05:51,150
That's weird.

3949
04:06:05,020 --> 04:06:05,820
There we go.

3950
04:06:06,360 --> 04:06:07,120
All right, man.

3951
04:06:08,480 --> 04:06:09,440
That was fun.

3952
04:06:11,700 --> 04:06:12,600
Patata, Oliver?

3953
04:06:12,980 --> 04:06:13,820
What does that mean?

3954
04:06:14,520 --> 04:06:15,960
I mean, it means potato, of course.

3955
04:06:17,520 --> 04:06:18,940
But why are you saying that?

3956
04:06:23,680 --> 04:06:24,520
Explain yourself.

3957
04:06:31,400 --> 04:06:33,020
Hi Oliver, it's fun watching you play.

3958
04:06:33,200 --> 04:06:34,920
Thank you, pretty microbiologist.

3959
04:06:38,120 --> 04:06:39,760
A new Slugcat campaign is out.

3960
04:06:39,880 --> 04:06:40,240
Oh yeah!

3961
04:06:41,160 --> 04:06:45,420
I did see that they were gonna put it out at some point, but I didn't realize it was already out.

3962
04:06:47,220 --> 04:06:47,940
Is it any good?

3963
04:06:58,820 --> 04:06:59,640
Came out today.

3964
04:06:59,860 --> 04:07:00,540
Did you all play it?

3965
04:07:03,920 --> 04:07:06,760
You called our cute Scottish Highland cattle a buffalo.

3966
04:07:09,300 --> 04:07:09,920
I did?

3967
04:07:10,580 --> 04:07:11,480
Well, wasn't it?

3968
04:07:12,120 --> 04:07:13,420
Well, I guess it wasn't a buffalo.

3969
04:07:16,450 --> 04:07:16,810
Really?

3970
04:07:16,890 --> 04:07:17,450
They look like that?

3971
04:07:17,610 --> 04:07:19,450
I don't know a lot about biology, okay?

3972
04:07:20,450 --> 04:07:22,070
Listen, Jim, I'm not a biologist.

3973
04:07:22,070 --> 04:07:23,110
I'm a physicist, okay?

3974
04:07:26,670 --> 04:07:27,430
Silksong came out.

3975
04:07:27,530 --> 04:07:28,030
Are you gonna play it?

3976
04:07:28,030 --> 04:07:28,490
No, it didn't.

3977
04:07:29,090 --> 04:07:29,770
You're lying.

3978
04:07:31,590 --> 04:07:33,430
But if it did come out, I would play it.

3979
04:07:33,790 --> 04:07:37,090
Well, not right now, but... ASAP, you know?

3980
04:07:38,950 --> 04:07:40,030
It's a Highland cow.

3981
04:07:41,250 --> 04:07:41,610
Oh.

3982
04:07:43,620 --> 04:07:45,040
It was the Nintendo Direct?

3983
04:07:45,280 --> 04:07:45,420
What?

3984
04:07:48,040 --> 04:07:49,360
I don't even know what you're talking about.

3985
04:07:49,820 --> 04:07:50,980
Silksong came... No, no, no.

3986
04:07:51,060 --> 04:07:52,140
It didn't come out, guys.

3987
04:07:53,340 --> 04:07:54,180
Deltarune Tomorrow?

3988
04:07:57,200 --> 04:07:59,460
Assume a special... a spherical buffalo.

3989
04:07:59,760 --> 04:08:01,240
Now you're getting it!

3990
04:08:02,880 --> 04:08:05,440
I like patata, and I like Oliver, so I mixed it.

3991
04:08:05,780 --> 04:08:06,380
Well, that's funny.

3992
04:08:06,420 --> 04:08:08,480
I also like myself, and I like patata.

3993
04:08:09,700 --> 04:08:11,480
So we both have that in common.

3994
04:08:12,120 --> 04:08:13,140
I also like you.

3995
04:08:13,480 --> 04:08:13,920
Theoplia?

3996
04:08:14,700 --> 04:08:16,080
Or is it Theoplia?

3997
04:08:20,660 --> 04:08:22,580
Yeah, what got the leaders?

3998
04:08:23,080 --> 04:08:24,100
Was it something bad?

3999
04:08:26,860 --> 04:08:29,580
If it was the thing about the Highland Cow, it's not real.

4000
04:08:29,660 --> 04:08:30,040
It's fine.

4001
04:08:30,520 --> 04:08:31,320
That's not a spoiler.

4002
04:08:33,340 --> 04:08:35,720
But I like that you're being overly cautious, though.

4003
04:08:39,800 --> 04:08:42,560
That was my first time hearing the new sounds in the desert.

4004
04:08:42,720 --> 04:08:43,000
Really cool.

4005
04:08:43,220 --> 04:08:43,580
Right?

4006
04:08:44,460 --> 04:08:46,140
It's one of the best things ever they added!

4007
04:08:47,780 --> 04:08:51,820
A lot of the times when these updates come out, I'm not really sure what has changed.

4008
04:08:54,100 --> 04:08:58,900
But I think I've played the game enough now that if something changes, I will notice it.

4009
04:09:00,060 --> 04:09:02,500
And not just think, oh, I haven't seen this one before, you know?

4010
04:09:03,480 --> 04:09:03,880
Mostly.

4011
04:09:07,500 --> 04:09:10,720
By the way, I think the song you were thinking of was Switchback by Cell Dweller.

4012
04:09:13,480 --> 04:09:15,500
Yeah, I mean, that would make sense.

4013
04:09:16,560 --> 04:09:20,480
It's like a robotic voice when they go Switchback, you know?

4014
04:09:22,560 --> 04:09:24,380
Can you list things you noticed from the new update?

4015
04:09:24,580 --> 04:09:25,640
Uh, sounds in the desert.

4016
04:09:26,540 --> 04:09:27,860
I'm assuming the new cows.

4017
04:09:28,420 --> 04:09:29,060
Or whatever.

4018
04:09:29,960 --> 04:09:33,880
Maybe also the... demon chicken I saw.

4019
04:09:34,650 --> 04:09:35,870
That was very Demon.

4020
04:09:36,650 --> 04:09:38,050
Definitely part of the update.

4021
04:09:39,390 --> 04:09:43,270
And... The audio, right?

4022
04:09:43,410 --> 04:09:44,710
The 3D audio got fixed.

4023
04:09:44,950 --> 04:09:45,350
Finally.

4024
04:09:45,690 --> 04:09:46,630
Which is awesome.

4025
04:09:47,310 --> 04:09:49,290
I really felt a difference in combat.

4026
04:09:49,490 --> 04:09:52,250
I could tell where things were much more easily now.

4027
04:09:58,310 --> 04:09:59,270
That bush you found!

4028
04:09:59,390 --> 04:10:00,310
Oh yeah, yeah, that's right!

4029
04:10:00,510 --> 04:10:02,070
The firefly bush was amazing!

4030
04:10:02,290 --> 04:10:03,890
That one was definitely part of the update.

4031
04:10:06,850 --> 04:10:09,190
By the way, that new music you heard was there all along.

4032
04:10:09,330 --> 04:10:10,270
Rareest track in the game.

4033
04:10:10,370 --> 04:10:10,990
No shit!

4034
04:10:12,570 --> 04:10:14,250
Now I'm just wondering what else I missed.

4035
04:10:17,810 --> 04:10:18,530
Damn ads!

4036
04:10:19,470 --> 04:10:21,650
I mean, if only there was a way to disable them, you know?

4037
04:10:22,690 --> 04:10:25,670
You can probably use some kind of ad blocker.

4038
04:10:27,370 --> 04:10:28,170
It should work.

4039
04:10:30,630 --> 04:10:33,870
Hey Oliver, have you ever considered streaming at variated times?

4040
04:10:34,070 --> 04:10:36,770
I'm sure there's a whole community of viewers who can't ever get to this one.

4041
04:10:37,210 --> 04:10:39,250
You know, that's actually a really good point, Reef.

4042
04:10:41,290 --> 04:10:46,510
I have especially been thinking about it lately because of my neighbor that always starts to play music when I start streaming.

4043
04:10:47,090 --> 04:10:49,930
So I thought maybe I should start earlier when he's at work, you know?

4044
04:10:50,590 --> 04:10:52,370
Then he's also not gonna be annoyed by me.

4045
04:10:53,870 --> 04:10:55,050
Maybe I will switch it up.

4046
04:10:55,550 --> 04:10:57,110
Have, like, certain time slots.

4047
04:10:58,230 --> 04:11:00,290
Maybe, uh, back and forth, you know?

4048
04:11:00,810 --> 04:11:03,270
Maybe one stream four hours earlier and then this stream?

4049
04:11:05,330 --> 04:11:06,150
Something like that.

4050
04:11:08,690 --> 04:11:09,930
What about noon for you?

4051
04:11:11,490 --> 04:11:12,790
So what is that in America?

4052
04:11:14,650 --> 04:11:16,030
That's like eight hours before that.

4053
04:11:16,210 --> 04:11:17,610
That's like in the middle of the night.

4054
04:11:22,520 --> 04:11:23,800
Oh, morning, I guess, yeah.

4055
04:11:26,560 --> 04:11:28,600
I think I would try it.

4056
04:11:28,780 --> 04:11:29,420
See how it goes.

4057
04:11:30,260 --> 04:11:36,460
It would be really cool to see if there's a bunch of new people that are never able to tune in, right?

4058
04:11:36,580 --> 04:11:37,580
Because of the time zones.

4059
04:11:39,280 --> 04:11:41,460
Maybe you should decrease your simulation distance a bit.

4060
04:11:41,560 --> 04:11:43,040
It causes some of the lag you notice.

4061
04:11:43,900 --> 04:11:45,640
I haven't noticed any lag today at all.

4062
04:11:46,440 --> 04:11:48,460
It has been completely smooth today.

4063
04:11:52,750 --> 04:11:56,030
I'm asking that because your stream time in Australia is 2 a.m.

4064
04:11:56,230 --> 04:11:58,530
Ah, right.

4065
04:12:00,670 --> 04:12:01,710
It's 5 p.m.

4066
04:12:01,770 --> 04:12:02,850
here in Ohio.

4067
04:12:03,610 --> 04:12:08,790
Yeah, so when I stream at 6 in my time, so 6 p.m.

4068
04:12:08,870 --> 04:12:16,270
in the evening, it's a really good time for, well, Europeans, of course, because I assume most people are home from work at that time.

4069
04:12:16,790 --> 04:12:17,910
You know, 9 to 5.

4070
04:12:19,610 --> 04:12:20,090
And...

4071
04:12:20,250 --> 04:12:25,390
People in the US are, I guess, working, but they have the option somehow, maybe some of them to tune in.

4072
